---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="A look behind the screen — what drives me, what I value, and what I tinker with."
  pageClass="page-red"
>
  <h1>whoami</h1>
  <p class="full-width">
    A quick look at who’s behind the screen. You can read about all the
    work-related skills and achievments from the <a href="/experience/"
      >experience-page</a
    >, but who is Arttu really and what does he do on his free time? Read and
    find out!
  </p>

  <hr />

  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>🎧 Hobbies & Interests</h2>

      <p>
        Some would say I collect hobbies, but I myself say that I just enjoy a
        lot of different things.
      </p>

      <p>
        Latest one is <strong>DJ'ing</strong>: started it in March 2025. Still
        very much in the beginner zone, but I've already fallen into the world
        of spinning decks. It's an excellent way to spend time: you constantly
        bump into good music, connect with like-minded people and it is relaxing
        to just concentrate on the music!
      </p>

      <p>
        I've also picked up <a
          href="https://arttu.net/blog/running-with-suunto-run/">running</a
        > after many, many years of pause. Slowly trying to get back into the shape
        in which I was 10 years ago.
      </p>

      <p>
        In the summer I like to go <strong>magnet fishing</strong>. Low effort,
        weirdly satisfying. Feels like a treasure hunt, especially fun with
        friends.
      </p>

      <p>
        I enjoy <strong>reading books</strong> a lot: mostly biographies, tech-related
        history pieces and stuff about weird or esoteric stuff. I <strong
          >watch movies and tv-shows</strong
        >
        a lot — mostly sci-fi, thrillers, horror and anime.
      </p>

      <p>
        Then there's also <strong>hiking</strong>, <strong>puzzles</strong>, <strong
          >playing guitar</strong
        > — the list goes on. I won't pretend I do them all regularly, but they're
        all there from time to time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-visual">
      <svg
        class="about-svg"
        viewBox="0 0 120 120"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      >
        <circle cx="30" cy="30" r="30" fill="var(--accent)"></circle>
        <circle
          cx="80"
          cy="80"
          r="20"
          fill="var(--color-bg)"
          stroke="var(--accent)"
          stroke-width="6"></circle>
        <path
          d="M 0 100 Q 60 60 120 100"
          stroke="var(--accent)"
          stroke-width="5"
          fill="none"></path>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-section reverse">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>🧠 Tech & Tinkering</h2>

      <p>
        I started coding early — when websites still used table layouts and
        blinking text. First projects were in pure HTML and CSS, and I built
        little games with CoolBasic. None of them survived. I kind of wish they
        did.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm into tech history: things like “why VHS beat Betamax” or “what
        killed Symbian”. I think those stories tell a lot about how humans,
        systems and decisions mix.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've messed around with different OSes, run a home Linux server, and
        started countless side projects. Many based on a joke. Most unfinished.
        Fun while they lasted. Some of them can be found from my <a
          href="/projects/">projects</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-visual">
      <svg
        class="about-svg"
        viewBox="0 0 120 120"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      >
        <rect x="10" y="10" width="40" height="40" fill="var(--accent)"></rect>
        <rect
          x="60"
          y="60"
          width="50"
          height="50"
          fill="none"
          stroke="var(--accent)"
          stroke-width="5"
          rx="10"></rect>
        <line
          x1="10"
          y1="110"
          x2="110"
          y2="10"
          stroke="var(--accent)"
          stroke-width="4"></line>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>🧭 What I Value</h2>

      <p>
        I like figuring things out — in tech, people, systems, stories. I like
        weird ideas, and I think the best way to learn is to first get the
        background information and then just trying things out.
      </p>
      <p>
        I admire people who are genuinely into things. Doesn't matter what:
        jazz, insects, obscure programming languages. Passion is cool.
      </p>
      <p>
        I respect people who treat others as people — regardless of title, role,
        or status. It matters to me that someone can stay grounded and human,
        both in day-to-day life and professional setting.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-visual">
      <svg
        class="about-svg"
        viewBox="0 0 120 120"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      >
        <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="25" fill="var(--accent)"></circle>
        <line
          x1="60"
          y1="0"
          x2="60"
          y2="120"
          stroke="var(--accent)"
          stroke-width="4"></line>
        <line
          x1="0"
          y1="60"
          x2="120"
          y2="60"
          stroke="var(--accent)"
          stroke-width="4"></line>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr />

  <p>
    If any of this feels familiar, you’ll probably enjoy my <a href="/blog/"
      >blog</a
    >.
  </p>

  <style>
    .about-section {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 4rem;
      margin-bottom: 6rem;
    }

    .about-section.reverse {
      direction: rtl;
    }

    .about-section.reverse > * {
      direction: ltr;
    }

    .about-text {
      max-width: 65ch;
    }

    .about-visual {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 100%;
      height: 100%;
    }

    .about-svg {
      width: 120px;
      height: 120px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .about-section,
      .about-section.reverse {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        direction: ltr;
      }

      .about-visual {
        margin-top: 0rem;
        min-height: auto;
        height: auto;
      }
    }

    .about-svg {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(20px) scale(0.95);
      transition: all 0.6s ease-out;
    }

    .about-svg.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("visible");
        }
      });
    },
    {
      threshold: 0.6,
    }
  );

  document.querySelectorAll(".about-svg").forEach((el) => {
    observer.observe(el);
  });
</script>
